[00:00.00]Today we're going to practice listening and understanding English by talking about chores.|今天我们用聊「家务」来练习英语听力和理解。
[00:04.64]Talking about chores.|聊聊家务。
[00:06.88]Chores are routine tasks that you have to do, usually at home.|家务就是你日常必须做的琐事，通常是在家里。
[00:11.06]People need to do many chores at home every week.|人们每周在家都要做很多家务。
[00:14.04]Adults do chores, and many kids do chores too.|大人做家务，很多孩子也做。
[00:17.66]This isn't the most fun topic, but it's an important one.|这不是最有趣的话题，但很重要。
[00:21.44]You'll probably learn some new words in this video.|这期视频里你大概能学到一些新词。
[00:24.74]Chores as a kid.|小时候的家务。
[00:26.36]When I was a kid, I did a few different chores at home.|我小时候在家做几种家务。
[00:30.68]I was lucky because I didn't have to do a lot.|我挺幸运的，因为要做的不多。
[00:33.62]Some of my friends did many chores.|我有些朋友要做很多家务。
[00:35.98]I remember that my neighbor did many different tasks for hours every weekend.|我记得我的邻居每个周末都要干好几个小时的各种活儿。
[00:40.56]He cleaned many parts of his house, his front yard, and his backyard.|他要打扫房子里很多地方、前院和后院。
[00:45.16]I didn't do that much.|我没做那么多。
[00:47.04]But, for example, I had to clean my room often.|但比如说，我得经常打扫自己的房间。
[00:51.10]This is one chore that most children need to do.|这是大多数孩子都要做的一项家务。
[00:54.54]We're responsible for our bedroom.|我们要对自己的卧室负责。
[00:57.30]We have to organize things and put things away.|我们得整理东西，把东西收好。
[01:01.72]Cleaning and organizing.|打扫和整理。
[01:04.24]Put things away means that you put things where they belong,|「把东西收好」的意思是放回它们该在的地方，
[01:07.32]like in the closet, dresser, or on the desk.|比如衣柜里、抽屉柜里，或者桌子上。
[01:10.76]When I was a kid, I liked keeping my room organized.|我小时候喜欢把房间收拾得整整齐齐。
[01:13.74]I never left my toys or clothes on the floor.|我从不把玩具或衣服丢在地上。
[01:17.80]Taking out the trash.|倒垃圾。
[01:20.30]Another chore that I did was taking the trash out.|我做的另一项家务是倒垃圾。
[01:23.28]When the trash bags were full, I took them to our big trash bins.|垃圾袋满了，我就把它们拿去大垃圾桶。
[01:26.36]these are the big containers where you put trash.|那是装垃圾的大容器。
[01:29.96]In the United States, the garbage truck comes once a week to collect your trash.|在美国，垃圾车每周来一次收垃圾。
[01:34.14]So I had to take the trash bins to the curb the night before.|所以我得在前一天晚上把垃圾桶推到路边。
[01:37.72]The curb is the edge of the sidewalk next to the street.|「Curb」就是人行道挨着马路的那条边。
[01:41.78]Cleaning the bathroom|打扫浴室。
[01:42.74]Nowadays, I still take the trash out every week.|现在，我每周仍然要倒垃圾。
[01:46.92]I don't mind this chore.|这项家务我不介意。
[01:48.82]It's easy for me, but one chore I don't like is cleaning the bathroom.|对我来说很简单，但有一项我不喜欢——打扫浴室。
[01:52.78]This was the worst thing I had to do when I was young.|这是我小时候最讨厌做的活儿。
[01:56.36]I'm not good at things like this, and it always took me a long time to finish.|这类事我不在行，每次都要花很久才能做完。
[02:01.90]In particular, I hated cleaning the toilet.|我尤其讨厌刷马桶。
[02:04.92]I always thought this was a little gross or disgusting.|我总觉得那有点恶心。
[02:08.62]How about you? Do you like cleaning the bathroom?|你呢？你喜欢打扫浴室吗？
[02:12.46]Bringing in the newspaper.|拿报纸。
[02:14.52]The easiest chore that I did as a kid was bringing the newspaper inside.|我小时候最轻松的家务就是把报纸拿进屋。
[02:19.12]Every morning I went out to get the newspaper, which was always on the ground in front of our house.|每天早上我出去拿报纸，它总是放在我家门前的地上。
[02:23.92]I always brought it inside for my parents|我总是帮父母把它拿进屋。
[02:26.98]But nowadays, fewer people read physical newspapers|但如今，看纸质报纸的人越来越少了，
[02:31.26]So it's not the same|所以情况不一样了。
[02:32.94]I don't see many newspapers in front of people's houses|我很少看到别人家门口有报纸了。
[02:36.96]Skimming the pool|捞泳池。
[02:38.96]One other chore that I had to do was skimming the pool|我还要做的另一项家务是捞泳池。
[02:42.26]Skimming the pool means cleaning the surface or top of the water|「捞泳池」就是清理水面的漂浮物。
[02:46.48]My family had a pool in the backyard and it got pretty dirty|我家后院有个泳池，很容易变脏，
[02:50.32]There were always leaves, bugs, and other things|总是有树叶、虫子之类的东西，
[02:53.76]so I had to skim the pool.|所以我得把水面捞干净。
[02:56.80]Allowance|零花钱。
[02:57.32]One other important thing about chores|关于家务，还有一件重要的事，
[03:00.46]is that children usually earn an allowance when they do them.|那就是孩子做家务通常能拿到零花钱。
[03:04.16]An allowance is money that parents give to their children.|「Allowance」就是父母给孩子的钱。
[03:07.88]Usually, if children do all their chores, they get this reward.|通常孩子把家务都做完，就能得到这份奖励。
[03:12.46]I earned a little allowance when I was a kid.|我小时候也能赚到一点零花钱。
[03:15.26]I used this money to buy things that I wanted.|我用这些钱买自己想要的东西。
[03:18.66]Teaching responsibility|培养责任感。
[03:20.04]Many parents like giving their children an allowance because it teaches them that hard work pays off.|很多父母愿意给孩子零花钱，因为这能让孩子明白「努力会有回报」。
[03:27.30]This means that if you work hard, you'll get a reward afterward.|意思是：你努力了，之后就会有回报。
[03:31.04]It also teaches children that everyone has to work if they want to make money.|它也让孩子懂得：想赚钱，人人都得付出劳动。
[03:35.58]You can't earn money if you don't do anything.|什么都不做，就赚不到钱。
[03:38.30]With chores and allowance, children learn responsibility, and they learn how to work hard in the future.|通过家务和零花钱，孩子学会了责任，也学会了将来如何努力工作。
[03:44.80]I want my kids to do chores so they can learn these lessons too.|我希望我的孩子也做家务，这样他们也能学到这些。
[03:48.62]Conclusion|结语。
[03:50.48]Chores are an important part of life.|家务是生活的重要部分。
[03:53.74]They help teach responsibility, and they make sure our homes stay clean and organized.|它们能培养责任感，也让我们的家保持整洁有序。
